BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Civic Reads: A Conversation with Author J.J. Green and Champlain C
 ollege President Alex Hernandez
DTSTART:20260924T183000
DTEND:20260924T200000
DTSTAMP:20260924T155103Z
UID:1c44c3428c1afd5e0380c2ccf1deed@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an insightful evening with the author of The Noise
  War: How to Find the Truth When Everything Is Lying to You\, a field manu
 al for a world where facts are under siege and lies travel faster than lig
 ht. Author J.J. Green distills two decades of frontline reporting from Kab
 ul to Kyiv\, from the Pentagon to the digital frontiers of influence warfa
 re\, into a clear\, practical guide for journalists\, policymakers\, educa
 tors\, and citizens determined to defend truth in an era of synthetic medi
 a and algorithmic manipulation. Please register at https://fletcherfree.li
 bcal.com/event/17386935\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Fletcher Free Library\, 235 College St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/civic-read
 s-a-conversation-with-author-j-j-green-and-champlain-college-president-ale
 x-hernandez-27-08-2026-12-57-38
END:VEVENT
