BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:OCM Festival String Quartet
DTSTART:20260924T193000
DTEND:20260924T213000
DTSTAMP:20260924T155103Z
UID:d99ba1bba2831ffe4a2da0910d43df@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Our inaugural chamber music concert explores this year's festi
 val theme through works that illuminate composers living under oppressive 
 regimes\, characters confronting profound personal struggles\, and music t
 hat embodies tension\, resilience\, and hope. Guided by Maestro Filippo Ci
 abatti\, this program spans masterpieces by Bach\, Purcell\, Schumann\, an
 d Shostakovich\, works by Rebecca Clarke\, Jessie Montgomery\, Shelley Was
 hington\, and George Walker\, and arrangements by Vermont composers Matthe
 w LaRocca and Kyle Saulnier. Featuring the OCM Festival String Quartet: Co
 ncertmaster Brooke Quiggins\, violin\; Joana Genova\, violin\; Stefanie Ta
 ylor\, viola\; and John Dunlop\, cello\, and mezzo-soprano Claire McCahan 
 and baritone Adam Richardson from the Rappahannock County production. Plus
 \, join us for an enlightening pre-concert talk with OCM Board Member and 
 Middlebury College musicologist Dr. Danielle Simon. Town Hall Theater\n\nS
 ources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/ocm-festiv
 al-string-quartet-15-09-2026-13-41-53
END:VEVENT
